READ ME
explanation to "Monte Carlo" type inversion
The sequence of programms creates a predefined number of starting models by semi-random pertubation of an initial 1D model. Semi-random means to express that the initial 1D model is only perturbed with in a predefined range of depth and velocities per layer. Currently, models that can be created consist of 3 layers under the seafloor. As the 1D model is "hung" under a bathymetric profile for the generation of the models
The created starting models are also 1D models and are subsequently inverted individually, using the same inversion parameters. Bad inversions with insufficient chi^2 and rms values can be excluded from the final averaging using exclude_badModels.sh
A mean model and thus the final model  can be calculated from the resulting inverted models using harmonic_mean_average.sh

Programm is started using make_stoch_models.sh, which then calls run_monte_inversion.sh which calls exclude_badModels.sh as well as standard inversion codes and finally calls Harmonic_mean_average.sh
